8. Dot Product
The dot product of two vectors u and v is defined as the scalar
u • v = v • u = u1v1 + u2v2 + u3v3 = ui vi .
It is easy to show that u • v = uv cos θ , where u and v are the magnitudes and θ is the angle between the vectors. The dot product is therefore the magnitude of one vector times the component of the other in the direction of the first. Clearly, the dot product u • v is equal to the sum of the diagonal terms of the tensor uivj .


